Amazon Prime Video &#x2019;s &#x201C;Melania: The Series&#x201D; offers a peek into the often-reclusive first lady&#x2019;s personal life and role inside the White House, including her efforts to provide children in foster care with educational and career opportunities.

But as the first lady seeks a more public-facing role in international peacemaking efforts, most recently taking credit for brokering a ceasefire in Ukraine , how often does she think about the children in Gaza, Israel and other parts of the world affected by conflict? blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Jeon Do-yeon on Oscar Contender 'Possible Love,' Korean Cinema's Commercial Pull and Her 'Greater Thirst' for Stories 'The Body' Creator on the Dance Team's Sexuality, What Happened to Grace and Whether God Is Real

When posed the question at the New York premiere of her new two-part Amazon series, the first lady told Variety : &#x201C;I want peace all around the world. That&#x2019;s very important to me. We should all live in harmony and peace.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I hope we can,&#x201D; she added, before vaguely suggesting how that peace might be achieved: &#x201C;To get together.&#x201D;

The first lady&#x2019;s call for peace comes at a pivotal moment in President Donald Trump &#x2019;s presidency, one where he attempts to recast himself as a global peacemaker after a bruising midterm defeat . (In the wake of the &#x201C;blue wave,&#x201D; Vice President JD Vance identified &#x201C;end[ing] the war&#x201D; and &#x201C;chang[ing] our relationship to Israel&#x201D; as two of the &#x201C;top four causes&#x201D; he and his most trusted pollsters believe could win back Republican voters who flipped their votes.)

Efforts &#x201C;to get together&#x201D; were underway just hours before the Prime Video series premiere, as Presidents Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin convened for a historic trilateral summit in China. The meeting culminated in a joint declaration emphasizing peace, commitments to the United Nations and a reaffirmation that &#x201C;a nuclear war cannot be won and must never be fought.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

While Trump celebrated the meeting as a historic breakthrough (fittingly rating his trip a &#x201C;12&#x201D; out of 10), some foreign policy analysts argued that the summit was more spectacle than substance and raised concerns over legitimizing Putin without securing concessions on Ukraine. The joint declaration also did not directly address the ongoing conflicts in Gaza or Iran.

The two-part docuseries is the second project released under Amazon&#x2019;s $40 million licensing agreement for the Brett Ratner-directed &#x201C;Melania&#x201D; documentary, which debuted in January. Producer Marc Beckman oversaw the bidding war for what he calls &#x201C;the biggest documentary in history.&#x201D; (While the film exceeded box office expectations , its $16.6 million worldwide gross falls far short of the all-time documentary record. To put it in perspective, Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim&#x2019;s &#x201C;You Can See Everything&#x201D; earned more in its second weekend playing in U.S. theaters alone than &#x201C;Melania&#x201D; did during its entire worldwide run.)

&#x201C;I went to multiple entities, from Amazon to Netflix to Hulu to Paramount, and all of them were interested in picking up the film,&#x201D; Beckman said. &#x201C;I can tell you point-blank, Amazon&#x2019;s team was honestly the best in Hollywood. They understood how important it was to get this story out. It's a piece of history. It's never been told before, and we were really impressed with the leadership at Amazon. Really great people.&#x201D;

Did Jeff Bezos participate? &#x201C;No, he never was involved,&#x201D; Beckman claimed. &#x201C;He wasn&#x2019;t involved in the negotiation, and he wasn&#x2019;t involved in anything else.&#x201D; (Democratic lawmakers, including Sen. Elizabeth Warren, have accused Bezos&#x2019; company of &#x201C;bribery in plain sight,&#x201D; alleging that Amazon vastly overpaid for the rights and outbid its rivals by a wide margin to curry favor with the Trump administration. Bezos defended the purchase as &#x201C;a very wise business decision.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Melania: The Series&#x201D; is now streaming on Prime Video.

Bassam Tariq is opening up about what he learned working on Marvel 's scrapped Blade reboot.

In an interview with The New Arab published Friday, the Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother director was asked what his time working in the "studio system" taught him about how he wants to approach filmmaking. Tariq said it felt "dangerous" to begin casting without "a proper script," and that he prefers to "have full control over my script."

"It was funny and strange to start casting and building without a proper script. You're sitting there and explaining to actors what their role will be, and they just have to believe you," he said. "That's also very dangerous because if the text comes and it doesn't add up to what you were saying, your credibility gets completely shot. All I have is my integrity, and I've been thinking about that a lot." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Hollywood Flashback When Kevin Feige Got Off to a Less-Than-Incredible Start at Marvel TV 'VisionQuest' Creator Terry Matalas Tells All About That Supersized Finale and Post-Credits Surprise

In 2021, it was reported that Tariq was attached to helm Marvel's Blade film; Mahershala Ali was announced as the project's star seven years ago at Comic-Con 2019. The actor confirmed in a July interview with GQ that he would not be leading Blade .

The Hollywood Reporter exclusively reported in September 2022 that Tariq had exited the project, with the director saying in a statement at the time, &#x201C;It&#x2019;s been an honor working with the wonderful folks at Marvel. We were able to put together a killer cast and crew. Eager to see where the next director takes the film.&#x201D;

Tariq continued in his interview with The New Arab, "If you're the bearer of bad news to your actors, but you're not the one making any of these decisions &#x2014; and it's actually coming from a corporate entity &#x2014; that's not a great way to be a director. I know some people can take that and run with it, but I learned I was losing credibility with my actors, and it wasn't a healthy way to operate as a filmmaker." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In short, the director said his "big lesson" was that he wanted to have full control of the scripts of his films, noting "life's too short to make shit films." Tariq added, "If we disagree, it's between them and me. It's quite sad because we had such high hopes for what we wanted to build."

Ali said in a September interview with GQ that he agrees the failed film is Kevin Feige&#x2019;s "biggest failure."

When asked why the film didn&#x2019;t happen with the interviewer, the Oscar winner said, &#x201C;That&#x2019;s a Kevin Feige question.&#x201D; He continued, &#x201C;They had, as you said, a two-time Oscar-winning actor under contract and you got billions of dollars. That&#x2019;s a question for them. I don&#x2019;t mean anything personal to you, but I don&#x2019;t know why it didn&#x2019;t. To this day, I don&#x2019;t know why it didn&#x2019;t happen. I just know that it was &#x2014; Kevin, he said it was the biggest failure of his career and I agree.&#x201D;

Chris Columbus didn&#x2019;t know a new &#x201C; Home Alone &#x201D; was coming.

The director of the 1990 original spoke with Variety minutes before news broke that Disney is developing a new installment with Macaulay Culkin. According to sources, Columbus had no knowledge that the project was in development or about to be announced. When asked about the franchise&#x2019;s future, his answer was that any return faces a steep climb without Catherine O&#x2019;Hara. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Beast in Me' Season 2 Casts Riley Keough, Lorelei Olivia Mote, Aaron Paul, Taip Ceman, Matthew James Thomas Priyanka Chopra Jonas, Russell Crowe Sci-Fi Thriller 'Bluefly' Adds 'Beast' Star Daniel MacPherson (EXCLUSIVE)

&#x201C;Catherine, as I&#x2019;ve always said, is 50% of &#x2018;Home Alone,&#x2019;&#x201D; Columbus says. &#x201C;There&#x2019;s the yin and yang of &#x2018;Home Alone&#x2019;: Catherine O&#x2019;Hara and Macaulay Culkin. Without those two in the film, there is no film, because they create the emotional epicenter of that film.&#x201D;

O&#x2019;Hara, who played Kevin McCallister&#x2019;s mother, Kate, died Jan. 30 at 71.

As reported Friday , Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg are shaping the script with Culkin and will produce through their Point Grey banner. The project is in early development at Disney, and plot details and casting remain under wraps. According to Deadline, the film grew out of a pitch Culkin made to Disney film chief David Greenbaum, told from the point of view of an older Kevin as a father.

When Variety followed up after the announcement, Columbus declined to comment further.

Columbus, who is set to receive a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in December, was particularly warm about his former star&#x2019;s return to the role in a McDonald&#x2019;s holiday commercial released Nov. 17. &#x201C;I love Macaulay&#x2019;s McDonald&#x2019;s commercial,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;Macaulay is a great actor, and I hope to work with him on something. Maybe it&#x2019;ll be &#x2018;Home Alone&#x2019;-related, maybe it won&#x2019;t.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He leaves the door open to a return built around the original ensemble.

&#x201C;I think you potentially could still entertain the idea of doing another &#x2018;Home Alone&#x2019; with the cast,&#x201D; Columbus explains. &#x201C;Not any of these ridiculous follow-ups to the first. And I only say ridiculous because it&#x2019;s weird with filmmakers. They don&#x2019;t understand why that cast works so well. It&#x2019;s always about the cast. It&#x2019;s like &#x2018;The Goonies.&#x2019; It&#x2019;s about the cast.&#x201D;

The franchise continued without Culkin and Columbus in &#x201C;Home Alone 3&#x201D; (1997), &#x201C;Home Alone 4&#x201D; (2002), &#x201C;Home Alone: The Holiday Heist&#x201D; (2012) and Disney+&#x2019;s &#x201C;Home Sweet Home Alone&#x201D; (2021).

But Columbus says O&#x2019;Hara&#x2019;s death has changed what a reunion could be. &#x201C;It was really about Catherine and Macaulay, if anyone ever wanted to do a sequel,&#x201D; he says, &#x201C;and unfortunately that can&#x2019;t happen now.&#x201D;

He also makes the case for the film&#x2019;s burglars, Harry and Marv, played by Joe Pesci and Daniel Stern.

&#x201C;Let&#x2019;s not downsize Harry and Marv,&#x201D; Columbus says. &#x201C;Daniel Stern and Joe Pesci are the ultimate comic duo for that particular film. Everyone has tried in subsequent sequels to be as funny or as interesting as Dan and Joe, and they just had a chemistry that is undefinable. So you can&#x2019;t do that.&#x201D;

Columbus, who also directed 1992&#x2019;s &#x201C;Home Alone 2: Lost in New York,&#x201D; has long been skeptical of revisiting the property. In 2020, he told Insider that Disney&#x2019;s planned reboot was &#x201C;a waste of time&#x201D; and that &#x201C;nobody got in touch with me about it.&#x201D; That project became &#x201C;Home Sweet Home Alone.&#x201D; Last year, he told Entertainment Tonight that another &#x201C;Home Alone&#x201D; would be a &#x201C;mistake.&#x201D;

Rogen also has a personal connection to O&#x2019;Hara. She played studio executive Patty Leigh in his Apple TV comedy &#x201C;The Studio,&#x201D; a role she still held when she died. O&#x2019;Hara also spoke at Culkin&#x2019;s own Walk of Fame ceremony in December 2023.

Columbus is next set to direct &#x201C;Gremlins 3,&#x201D; which is scheduled to begin shooting early next year. He executive produced Robert Eggers&#x2019; upcoming horror film &#x201C;Werwulf,&#x201D; which Focus Features opens Dec. 25.

Taylor Swift certainly brought her fans with her back to Country Music&#x2019;s Biggest Night.

The 60th annual ceremony hit a seven-year audience high with 7.62 million total live + same-day viewers tuning in for the CMA Awards on Wednesday, per Nielsen Big Data + Panel.

The star-studded show, which featured Swift's return to the CMA stage after 13 years to perform a mash up of Toy Story 5 's "I Knew It, I Knew You" and her classic "Our Song," also managed a 1.01 rating among adults 18-49 &#x2014;&#xA0;a three-year best.

